## Controlled Encoded PowerShell Test

A harmless PowerShell command was converted to Base64 and executed using PowerShell's encoded-command functionality.

Payload:

```powershell
$cmd='Write-Output "Sprint21 DET003 Test"'
```

Encoding:

```powershell
$bytes=[Text.Encoding]::Unicode.GetBytes($cmd)
$encoded=[Convert]::ToBase64String($bytes)
```

Execution:

```powershell
powershell.exe -EncodedCommand $encoded
```

Expected output:

```text
Sprint21 DET003 Test
```

The command performed no malicious action.

Its purpose was to generate endpoint telemetry containing:

```text
powershell.exe
-EncodedCommand
```

for detection-engineering validation.

