# DET-003 Development

Created:

```text
DET-003 — Encoded PowerShell Execution
```

Detection objective:

> Identify PowerShell process executions containing encoded-command arguments that may warrant security investigation.

Primary behavior:

```text
PowerShell
    +
Encoded Command Argument
```

Basic search:

```spl
index=* ("-EncodedCommand" OR " -enc ")
```

Preferred Sysmon-based detection:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1
(CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*" OR CommandLine="* -enc *")
```

Portfolio output:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1
(CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*" OR CommandLine="* -enc *")
| eval detection="DET-003 - Encoded PowerShell Execution"
| table _time detection host User Image CommandLine
```

The exact process fields used by the detection were validated against the endpoint telemetry available in Splunk.

---

## Detection Logic

```text
Endpoint Process Creation
          |
          v
Is Process PowerShell?
          |
          v
Review Command Line
          |
          v
Encoded Argument Present?
       /          \
      NO          YES
      |            |
      v            v
No DET-003      DET-003
```

The detection identifies a suspicious execution characteristic rather than attempting to identify a specific offensive tool.

