# Analyst Investigation

When DET-003 triggers, the analyst should:

1. Identify the endpoint.
2. Identify the executing user.
3. Review the complete PowerShell command line.
4. Identify the parent process.
5. Review PowerShell Script Block telemetry when available.
6. Determine the purpose of the encoded command.
7. Review related process creation.
8. Review network activity.
9. Review child processes.
10. Determine whether execution was authorized.
11. Correlate with other detections.
12. Escalate unexplained or suspicious activity.

Workflow:

```text
DET-003 Triggered
        |
        v
Identify Endpoint
        |
        v
Identify User
        |
        v
Review Command Line
        |
        v
Review Parent Process
        |
        v
Review Script Block
        |
        v
