## Parent Process Investigation

Sysmon process telemetry can provide parent-process context.

Search:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1 "powershell"
| table _time host User ParentImage Image CommandLine
```

The parent process can help determine how PowerShell was launched.

Context should be evaluated rather than treating any individual parent process as inherently malicious.

---

## Script Block Correlation

PowerShell Script Block Logging can provide additional visibility into executed PowerShell content.

Search:

```spl
index=* EventCode=4104 host="WIN11-02"
```

For the controlled Sprint 21 tests, the analyst could search for:

```text
DET003
```

Correlation between:

```text
Sysmon Process Creation
          +
PowerShell Script Block Logging
```

provides stronger investigative context than either telemetry source alone.

---

## Network Correlation

Sysmon network telemetry can be reviewed around the time of the detection.

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" EventCode=3
```

The controlled Sprint 21 payload only generated local output and therefore was not expected to produce suspicious outbound network activity.

The absence or presence of related network connections can help the analyst determine the significance of a PowerShell detection.

---

## Process Correlation

Additional process-creation telemetry can be reviewed using:

```spl
index=* host="WIN11-02" EventCode=1
```

The analyst should determine whether PowerShell launched unusual child processes or whether additional suspicious execution occurred around the detection.

