# False Positive Considerations

Encoded or unusual PowerShell execution can occur legitimately.

Potential legitimate sources include:

- Administrative automation
- Configuration-management tools
- Deployment systems
- Software installers
- IT support scripts
- Security tools
- Developer workflows
- Authorized security testing

DET-003 should therefore be treated as an investigation signal rather than proof of compromise.

---

# Detection Tuning

Future tuning can incorporate additional context.

```text
Encoded PowerShell
       |
       +---- Unexpected Parent Process
       |
       +---- Suspicious Script Block
       |
       +---- Network Connection
       |
       +---- Unusual Child Process
       |
       +---- Sensitive User/Host
       |
       v
Higher Detection Confidence
```

A production detection could assign greater severity when encoded PowerShell is correlated with additional suspicious endpoint or network behavior.

